 - Right to erasure: deleting one conversation, deleting all of a student's conversations, or deleting the account removes rows physically (no soft delete) via the cascades above.
 - Visibility: a student sees a conversation (list, messages, citation text) only while enrolled in its subject; unenrolment deletes nothing, re-enrolment makes the conversations visible again, and the right to erasure (delete one or all) works regardless of enrolment.
 - Retention: conversation data lives until the user deletes it or the account is deleted. Application logs must not contain message content or document text.
-- Teacher statistics (change `activity-events-and-metrics`, switched off by default): computed on the fly from `conversations`, `messages`, `message_sources`, `enrollments` and `documents` for the teacher who owns the subject; aggregate only (no text, no student identifier, no per-student figure), every figure withheld below 5 distinct students, weekly cells over a window of at most 12 whole weeks, only students currently enrolled. Nothing is stored (no table, counter or event), so a deletion by a student lowers the next result and no migration is involved. Students must be told about it in the privacy text before it is enabled (TD-069).
+- Teacher statistics (change `activity-events-and-metrics`, switched off by default): computed on the fly from `conversations`, `messages`, `message_sources`, `enrollments` and `documents` for the teacher who owns the subject; aggregate only (no text, no student identifier, no per-student figure), every figure withheld below 5 distinct students, weekly cells over a window of at most 12 whole weeks, only students currently enrolled. Since P1 of `activity-privacy-hardening`: the active students, the two rates and the document figures cover the latest complete block of two weeks counted from Monday 2026-01-05, whatever the requested window, and only the weeks of it whose weekly cell is published; a weekly cell, the rates and a document figure are also withheld when one student holds more than half (provisional); only current documents are listed, because the sources of a deleted one keep only its file name; a rate is withheld unless each group of answers on its sides (and the retrieved-only ones when both rates are shown) could be shown by itself, which makes the rates rare in small classes; the rate of uncited answers is also withheld when a deleted document was cited or the answers citing a withheld document are too few. Open: the document figures can be subtracted from totals and rates (TD-069). **Availability, by design:** the summary is 0 to 14 days old and returns 14 to 28 days after a removal (mean 21); in a simulation a class of 8 students with a weekly activity near 50 % shows a summary in about 53 % of the reads (72 % with blocks of four weeks) and a class of 12 in about 92 % (98 %); smaller or quieter classes often read as not enough data. The block length and the thresholds are constants to review with the data of a pilot. Nothing is stored (no table, counter or event), so a deletion by a student lowers the next result and no migration is involved. Students must be told about it in the privacy text before it is enabled (TD-069).
 - Third-party processing: message text and retrieved chunks are sent to Gemini. This must be disclosed in the privacy policy shown at consent time.
 
