+### Requirement: The summary figures come from one fixed, complete block
+The response SHALL carry `summary_window`, the latest block of 2 whole weeks aligned to the fixed Monday 2026-01-05 (common to every subject) that has ended (one hour after its Sunday); `active_students`, both rates and the document figures SHALL be computed only over it, whatever `start` and `end` say. When the request holds no whole week, no such block exists, or it starts before the first Monday after the marker, `summary_window` and those figures SHALL be null.
+
+#### Scenario: Two subjects, the same blocks
+- **WHEN** two subjects are read on the same day
+- **THEN** both report the same `summary_window`
+
+#### Scenario: Start and end have no effect
+- **WHEN** the same subject is read with different `start` and `end` values that each hold a whole week
+- **THEN** the summary figures and `summary_window` are identical
+
+#### Scenario: The block appears when it has ended
+- **WHEN** a read is made on Monday at 00:59:59 UTC and another at 01:00:00 UTC after the second week of a block
+- **THEN** only the second read has that block as `summary_window`
+
+#### Scenario: No block yet
+- **WHEN** the marker is later than the start of the latest complete block, or the window has 0 weeks
+- **THEN** `summary_window` is null and the summary figures are null
+
+### Requirement: A block is never shown trimmed or in two versions
+A block that starts before the first Monday after the marker SHALL be withheld whole. A teacher who controls the timing of removals SHALL NOT be able to see the same block with and without a student, nor two overlapping blocks.
+
+#### Scenario: A removal inside a block
+- **WHEN** a student is removed during a block, and the block completes
+- **THEN** the block is not shown, and neither is the one displayed before the removal
+
+#### Scenario: A random sequence
+- **WHEN** reads, removals and re-enrolments are generated over 20 weeks with fixed seeds
+- **THEN** no block appears in two versions of its figures
+
+### Requirement: Two summaries never overlap
+For any two reads, `summary_window` SHALL be equal or disjoint, equal windows SHALL give identical summary figures, and the existing test of V3, unchanged, SHALL pass: windows that differ by a week give the same `active_students` and rates.
+
+#### Scenario: The vector of V3
+- **WHEN** the sixth student was active only in the first week of the latest block and two reads are one week apart
+- **THEN** the summary figures are equal, or belong to disjoint blocks, and the student is not recoverable
+
+#### Scenario: A later block
+- **WHEN** a read is made after the next block has ended
+- **THEN** its `summary_window` is disjoint from the previous one
+
+### Requirement: The summary covers only the weeks whose cell is published
+`summary_weeks` SHALL list the Mondays of the weeks of the block that pass the rule of the weekly cell (at least 5 distinct students and no student above 50 % of the week's questions, whatever the requested window), and `active_students`, both rates and the document figures SHALL be computed only over those weeks. With none, `summary_weeks` and those figures SHALL be null.
+
+#### Scenario: Both weeks publishable
+- **WHEN** both weeks of the block have 5 or more balanced students
+- **THEN** `summary_weeks` lists both Mondays
+
+#### Scenario: One week withheld
+- **WHEN** the first week has 4 students and the second has 6
+- **THEN** `summary_weeks` lists only the second and the figures cover only it
+
+#### Scenario: The series window excludes the block
+- **WHEN** the requested window does not contain the block
+- **THEN** the summary is the same as with a window that contains it
+
+### Requirement: A withheld week cannot be recovered from the summary
+The response SHALL be a function of the published weeks only: two worlds that differ only in the facts of a withheld week (its students, their volume, its answers) SHALL give identical responses, and the denominator of the rates SHALL equal the sum of the published cells of `summary_weeks`.
+
+#### Scenario: Four students change their volume
+- **WHEN** the four students of a withheld week ask twice as many questions
+- **THEN** the whole response is identical
+
+#### Scenario: A heavy student of a withheld week
+- **WHEN** the heavy student of a week withheld for dominance asks more questions
+- **THEN** the whole response is identical
+
+#### Scenario: The denominator
+- **WHEN** both rates and the published cells are read
+- **THEN** the only total consistent with the rates, within the covered weeks, is the sum of the published cells
+
+### Requirement: An ended block changes only by an erasure, a removal or a document deletion
+After the end of a block, no new fact SHALL change its summary; it SHALL change only when a student erases data (equal to the world in which the student never existed), when a student is removed (the block is then null) or when the teacher deletes a document (which only removes or withholds figures).
+
+#### Scenario: Later facts
+- **WHEN** questions are added after the end of a block and it is read again
+- **THEN** the summary of that block is identical
+
+#### Scenario: An erasure
+- **WHEN** a student erases their data after a block has been read
+- **THEN** the block equals the one of a world without that student
+
+### Requirement: Dominance withholds a figure that one student concentrates
+A weekly cell, the two rates and the figure of each document SHALL be null when one student contributes more than 50 % of it (provisional, not validated), counting the questions of the week, each group of answers that a rate lets a reader compute and the appearances of the document, in addition to the minimum group of 5. A published figure SHALL equal the true count. `active_students` has no dominance rule.
+
+#### Scenario: One heavy student
+- **WHEN** five students asked 50, 1, 1, 1 and 1 questions in a week
+- **THEN** the cell is null
+
+#### Scenario: The boundary
+- **WHEN** five students asked 4, 1, 1, 1 and 1 questions, and then 5, 1, 1, 1 and 1
